{"step_index":820,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:31:10Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-24T19:31:10-04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-24T19:31:10-04:00\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\nEngine: Paschalion -> [GREGORIAN]\r\nEngine Init: Logic=[royal_doors] | Internal Content=[json_db/stamford]\r\nEngine: Loaded 447 assets from .\\assets\\stamford\r\nEngine: Loaded pre-computed almanac for year 2026 (annual_almanac_royal_doors_2026.json)\r\n# TYPICON: MONDAY, AUGUST 24th, 2026.\r\n\r\nEUTYCHES - TONE IV.  \r\nSt. Eutyches  \r\nMonday service combined with that of St. Eutyches.  \r\nVestment colour: Bright (Red).  \r\n\r\n## DAILY VESPERS\r\n\r\nNo kathisma is appointed.  \r\nGlory... Doxastikon of the Saint; Both now: Theotokion from the Horologion or Octoechos.  \r\n<span class=\"rubric\">Daily Prokeimenon (Monday of the Octoechos), Tone IV:</span> <span class=\"sung-text\">\"The Lord hears me when I cry out to Him\"</span>  \r\n<blockquote class=\"verse\"><span class=\"rubric\">Stichos:</span> <span class=\"sung-text\">Whenever I called, the God of my justice heard me.</span></blockquote>  \r\n**At the Aposticha:** We sing 3 daily Aposticha from the Octoechos; Glory, Both now: Aposticha Theotokion.  \r\n**At the Dismissal Troparia:** Troparion of St. Eutyches; Glory, Both now: Dismissal Theotokion in Tone IV.  \r\n\r\n## SMALL COMPLINE\r\n\r\nCanon: Theotokos from the Octoechos.  \r\nTroparia: Monday Troparion from the Octoechos, Troparion of the Temple, *\"O God of our fathers...\"* and the following three troparia.  \r\n\r\n## MIDNIGHT OFFICE (DAILY)\r\n\r\nMidnight Troparia: Troparion of the weekday, Troparion of the Temple, Troparion of the Saint (if any), daily Theotokion.  \r\nPrayer of St. Mardarius.  \r\n\r\n## DAILY MATINS\r\n\r\n*At The Lord is God�* we sing the Troparion of St. Eutyches, twice; Glory, Both now: Dismissal Theotokion in the tone of the Saint's troparion and of the day of the week.  \r\n\r\nWe read Kathismata 4 and 5.  \r\n\r\nAfter the Kathismata (4 & 5): We sing the Sessional Hymns from the Octoechos.  \r\nAt the Canon: Order of the Canon: First Canon of the Octoechos with the Heirmos on 4; second Canon of the Octoechos on 4; Canon of the Saint on 6. Katavasia: Heirmos of the last canon (of the Saint) after Odes 3, 6, 8, and 9.  \r\n\r\nNote: At the 9th Ode, the priest censes as at Great Matins.  \r\nAt Ode IX, we sing the Magnification ('My soul magnifies the Lord...') and the refrains ('More honorable than the Cherubim...').  \r\n**At the Aposticha:** We sing 3 daily Aposticha from the Octoechos; Glory, Both now: Aposticha Theotokion.  \r\n**At the Dismissal Troparia:** Troparion of St. Eutyches; Glory, Both now: Dismissal Theotokion for Monday in Tone I.  \r\n\r\n## HOURS\r\n\r\nTroparia: First Hour � Day; Third & Ninth Hours � St. Eutyches; Sixth Hour � Temple. Kontakia: First Hour � Day; Third & Ninth Hours � St. Eutyches; Sixth Hour � Temple.  \r\n\r\n## DIVINE LITURGY OF ST. JOHN CHRYSOSTOM\r\n\r\nPsalms of Typica; Beatitudes on 6: 3 from the Octoechos, 3 from Ode III of the Saint.  \r\n**Troparia and Kontakia:**  \r\nTroparion of the Angels.  \r\nTroparion of St. Eutyches.  \r\nKontakion of the Angels.  \r\nGlory... Kontakion of St. Eutyches.  \r\nBoth now: Kontakion of the Temple.  \r\n**Prokeimenon:**  \r\n> Tone IV: \"The righteous shall rejoice in the Lord\"\r\n**Epistle:**  \r\n> of the day (Romans 7:14-8:2)\r\n**Alleluia:**  \r\n> Tone IV, with verses of the day.\r\n**Gospel:**  \r\n> of the day (Matthew 10:9-15)\r\n**Communion Hymn:** of the day: \"He maketh His angels spirits.\"  \r\n**Post-Communion Hymn:** \"We have seen the true light, we have received the heavenly Spirit...\"  \r\nDismissal: May Christ our true God...  \r\n\n"}
